    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0385" n="375" xml:id="pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/710: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Singapore</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Patton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Singapore</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-08T06:00:00+07:30">December 8, 1941—6
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 8—5:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>339. Japanese raided Singapore 4 a.m. today and airfield Tengah nearby. They also
                    landed troops at Kota Bharu, northern Kelantan and heavy fighting reported here.
                    Damages light here, no casualties reported among Americans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Patton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
